# --- secrets: never commit ---
# `.env` alone did NOT cover .env.bak / .env.local / .env.save, which is how
# a backup containing live API keys reached a commit. Ignore every .env
# variant, then re-allow the one file that is meant to be tracked:
# .env.example, which holds placeholders only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Credential vault (MORTIMER_CREDENTIAL_VAULT_PLAN.md S8): encrypted,
# but never committed anyway — same backup-file lesson as above.
*.vault
*.vault.lock

# Stray backups and editor/filesystem droppings that have previously been
# swept into commits alongside secrets.
*.bak
.fuse_hidden*

data/*.db
data/*.db-*
data/*.bak*
# GC7: nightly sqlite backups (scripts/backup_db.py)
data/backups/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
node_modules/
dist/
.coverage
.eval-logs/
.acceptance-scratch/
data/wakeword/
models/
logs/
# Speaker gate (MORTIMER_VOICE_ISOLATION_TIER12_PLAN.md Tier 2): the
# downloaded ECAPA model, Larry's voice profile, and live-path enrollment
# captures — a voiceprint and raw voice recordings must never be committed.
data/models/
data/speaker_profile.*
data/speaker_captures/

# Mac shell (MORTIMER_MODEL_DISCIPLINE_AND_MAC_SHELL_PLAN.md B5): Xcode/SPM
# build noise. macos/MortimerShell's source, Package.swift, and templates/
# are tracked; everything Xcode generates locally is not.
macos/**/.build/
macos/**/.swiftpm/
macos/**/xcuserdata/
macos/**/DerivedData/
macos/**/build/
macos/**/*.xcuserstate
_to_delete/

# Self-edit session worktrees (jarvis/selfedit/service.py) — never part of the user's checkout
data/selfedit_worktrees/
_to_delete_tarballs/

# GC10 (gap-closure plan, 2026-09-04) hygiene
# speaker/eval captures live under data/; a WAV at the root is a stray
*.wav
web/dist_verify*/

# stray verification renders dropped at the repo root (seam.png, delib.png)
/*.png
